    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear cornerstone of our offensive strategy. With a projection of 87.42, **Yordan Alvarez** is primed for a massive outing against Grayson Rodriguez, buoyed by an elite xwOBA of 0.474 and a favorable matchup that boosts his SP skill score by 19%. Following closely, **Caleb Durbin** (72.37) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.52) represent our highest-upside speed threats. **Caleb Durbin** benefits from a soft matchup against Jacob Lopez, while the optimizer heavily weighted **Pete Crow-Armstrong**'s dynamic platoon advantage and leadoff spot, even despite the presence of a tough arm in Dustin May. We are also capitalizing on **Trea Turner**'s reliable efficiency (66.99); his combination of leadoff utility and high-frequency SB probability against a pitcher with slow delivery mechanics remains a statistical lock for our 5x5 objectives.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Jacob Gonzalez** from the active lineup. With a score of 43.11, he sits just below our efficiency threshold compared to the rest of the infield corps. While he benefits from the SP skill boost against Eduardo Rodriguez, his projected bottom-of-the-order slot (#9) and the inherent risk of a lefty-lefty matchup significantly dragged down his value relative to the lineup-leading utility of **Junior Caminero** or **Colt Keith**. We continue to monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar** (43.22); while he maintains a start, his negative platoon split against Matthew Boyd keeps his ceiling capped. We are proceeding with caution regarding the \u201cLineup Pending\u201d designations for **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, and **Josh Smith**; should official lineups deviate significantly from these projections, we may be forced to swap in depth pieces like **Chase Meidroth** or **Carson Benge**, particularly given the 45% rain risk currently haunting **Carson Benge**\u2019s path to the field.",
